# Exclude everything not strictly required to build the server image.
# Without this, COPY . . in Dockerfile pulls the full backend context
# (including backend/bin/config.json with the plaintext JWT secret,
# local doc-server.exe, dev databases, etc.) into the builder layer,
# where it remains accessible via `docker history` / `docker save`.
# (Issue #10)

# Go build/test/cache
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.test
*.out

# Local backend/bin (config.json with secret, dev DB, uploads, logs, certs, backups)
bin/
!bin/.gitkeep

# CI / scripts not needed for runtime
scripts/
tests/
*.ps1
*.sh

# Frontend (lives in ../frontend)
frontend/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Docs / handover
.trae/
doc/
docs/
README.md

# Misc
*.md
!monitoring/README.md
*.yml.tmpl
*.yaml.tmpl
Dockerfile.dev
.dockerignore